  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Food Systems - Support to investments in Value Chains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A priority for food systems development in partner countries is to support sustainable value chains able to boost investments, create jobs and increase growth by taking into account the inclusion of women and youth and the environmental dimensions (climate change, biodiversity loss, soil degradation, water scarcity, contamination, etc.). This Action will provide high quality assistance to prepare for investment in agricultural value chains. Financial resources are key to secure investments in the agricultural sector. Specific technical expertise will be mobilised to provide financial intelligence, identify investment opportunities in prioritised value chains and develop blending opportunities/ vehicles (AGRINTEL). Also, robust Value Chain Analysis are required prior to investments. Based on requests from EU Delegations and partners, these analyses provide evidence-based information and help them invest in value chains and inform policy dialogue (VCA4D). Finally, technical support will be provided to improve the sustainability of the cocoa supply chain with countries of West Africa, the main producers of cocoa in the world (SCI). The action will enable quick reactions to the demands from HQ and Delegations, as well as provide quality assistance throughout policy, programme and project preparatory processes, in complementarity with relevant regional agri-food system programmes.</narrative>
  </description>
